1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:02,947
(Scenes with child actors were filmed
safely with guardians and staff present.)

2
00:00:06,406 --> 00:00:07,341
Mi Young.

3
00:00:12,145 --> 00:00:13,013
Mi Young.

4
00:00:13,432 --> 00:00:16,416
Let the staff handle the heavy lifting
and take a break.

5
00:00:16,917 --> 00:00:18,045
You have a baby to think about now.

6
00:00:18,225 --> 00:00:19,705
I'm really fine.

7
00:00:19,706 --> 00:00:22,556
Everyone is so busy.
How can I just sit on my hands?

8
00:00:23,299 --> 00:00:25,425
Hello.

9
00:00:25,592 --> 00:00:27,694
Did you like all the dresses
you tried on last time?

10
00:00:27,695 --> 00:00:30,430
We have a lot of new designs
from our latest line now.

11
00:00:30,452 --> 00:00:31,939
Why don't you try them on one more time?

12
00:00:34,797 --> 00:00:36,823
Won Ho, are you busy?

13
00:00:36,882 --> 00:00:39,504
Can't you tell?
I don't even have a second to breathe.

14
00:00:40,559 --> 00:00:42,309
But what about Mi Young?

15
00:00:42,812 --> 00:00:44,612
Is she going to be okay working like that?

16
00:00:45,979 --> 00:00:46,914
What's wrong with Mi Young?

17
00:00:46,965 --> 00:00:49,449
It's peak season, so we have been
really busy lately.

18
00:00:50,417 --> 00:00:51,752
But she is pregnant,

19
00:00:51,807 --> 00:00:54,087
so I'm worried she might be
pushing herself too hard.

20
00:00:54,621 --> 00:00:56,256
You're right.

21
00:00:56,890 --> 00:00:59,993
Come to think of it, I've been so busy
I haven't taken care of her.

22
00:01:00,360 --> 00:01:02,505
I should tell her to go home and rest.

23
00:01:02,506 --> 00:01:04,740
She will probably insist
on staying anyway.

24
00:01:04,831 --> 00:01:07,334
Then what am I supposed to do?
I can't just let her keep pushing herself.

25
00:01:07,701 --> 00:01:09,469
Why don't you get her
some herbal medicine?

26
00:01:10,334 --> 00:01:11,138
Herbal medicine?

27
00:01:11,411 --> 00:01:13,411
You know that Korean Medicine Clinic
you go to sometimes.

28
00:01:13,448 --> 00:01:14,041
Yes.

29
00:01:14,101 --> 00:01:16,944
Why don't you get something
for Mi Young there?

30
00:01:17,181 --> 00:01:18,812
Oh, right. That place is good.

31
00:01:18,855 --> 00:01:20,547
The doctor there is trustworthy too.

32
00:01:20,948 --> 00:01:23,770
You're more thoughtful than I am.

33
00:01:28,755 --> 00:01:29,556
Hello.

34
00:01:29,608 --> 00:01:30,975
I'm here to pick up some herbal medicine.

35
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:31,968
What's your name?

36
00:01:32,061 --> 00:01:34,494
It should be under the name Ji Won Ho.

37
00:01:34,888 --> 00:01:36,764
I'm here to pick it up for him.

38
00:01:36,857 --> 00:01:38,665
All right, hold on.

39
00:01:47,195 --> 00:01:48,642
Here you are.

40
00:01:48,662 --> 00:01:49,509
Thank you.

41
00:01:50,143 --> 00:01:51,282
That's all.

42
00:01:51,962 --> 00:01:55,716
I took that herbal medicine
straight to you back then.

43
00:01:58,542 --> 00:02:01,488
But did that medicine really cause...

44
00:02:02,325 --> 00:02:03,431
what happened to her back then?

45
00:02:03,451 --> 00:02:05,759
No. There must have been
some kind of mistake.

46
00:02:07,461 --> 00:02:09,252
You don't need to worry
about this anymore. Go on.

47
00:02:09,312 --> 00:02:10,130
You should get back to work.

48
00:02:10,897 --> 00:02:11,865
All right, then.

49
00:02:21,041 --> 00:02:22,959
- Are you satisfied now?
- Satisfied with what?

50
00:02:22,990 --> 00:02:24,990
You just heard what Kyung Tae said.

51
00:02:25,178 --> 00:02:27,178
The medicine you took three years ago...

52
00:02:27,281 --> 00:02:29,983
came straight from the clinic,
with nothing wrong with it.

53
00:02:30,521 --> 00:02:32,386
That clears up
the misunderstanding, right?

54
00:02:32,455 --> 00:02:34,221
How many times do I have to tell you?

55
00:02:34,315 --> 00:02:36,906
Dal Rae died because of that medicine.

56
00:02:39,559 --> 00:02:42,129
When you first said Dal Rae died
because of some medicine,

57
00:02:42,319 --> 00:02:44,031
I never even imagined you meant
the herbal medicine.

58
00:02:44,032 --> 00:02:44,897
Do you know why?

59
00:02:45,052 --> 00:02:47,300
Because there's no way
that medicine was harmful.

60
00:02:47,601 --> 00:02:50,537
I told the doctor over and over
that you were pregnant...

61
00:02:50,538 --> 00:02:54,808
and asked to make sure
the medicine was safe for you.

62
00:02:55,108 --> 00:02:58,011
I never should have taken that medicine.

63
00:02:59,279 --> 00:03:00,847
Then you should have
said something back then.

64
00:03:02,349 --> 00:03:04,349
Fine. Even if it was,

65
00:03:04,851 --> 00:03:06,386
what do you expect me to do about it now?

66
00:03:06,687 --> 00:03:08,789
It has been three years.
What am I supposed to do now?

67
00:03:09,256 --> 00:03:10,357
Apologize.

68
00:03:11,425 --> 00:03:12,026
What?

69
00:03:12,073 --> 00:03:15,327
Admit that Dal Rae died
because of your mistake...

70
00:03:15,382 --> 00:03:17,725
and apologize, even if it's too late.

71
00:03:17,779 --> 00:03:19,653
Apologize to Dal Rae.

72
00:03:20,467 --> 00:03:21,668
What would that change?

73
00:03:24,351 --> 00:03:25,338
If I do,

74
00:03:26,006 --> 00:03:28,108
would she somehow come back to life?

75
00:03:29,209 --> 00:03:30,353
Get out.

76
00:03:30,354 --> 00:03:31,364
Get out!

77
00:03:31,365 --> 00:03:32,875
I said get out!

78
00:03:32,876 --> 00:03:34,414
I was leaving anyway.

79
00:03:58,138 --> 00:03:59,473
Kang Kyung Tae.

80
00:04:03,558 --> 00:04:04,811
What's wrong?

81
00:04:07,347 --> 00:04:09,516
I would like to hear
what you have to say about this.

82
00:04:13,820 --> 00:04:15,021
Let's talk outside.

83
00:04:22,162 --> 00:04:22,996
I went there that day...

84
00:04:23,697 --> 00:04:25,499
because I was worried.

85
00:04:25,966 --> 00:04:28,101
I was afraid you might be planning...

86
00:04:28,655 --> 00:04:29,603
to do something terrible again.

87
00:04:29,803 --> 00:04:30,837
What did you say?

88
00:04:31,029 --> 00:04:33,206
Those scandal photos
of Ms. Baek and Calvin.

89
00:04:33,874 --> 00:04:35,008
You were behind them, weren't you?

90
00:04:37,210 --> 00:04:39,446
Because of that, both Ms. Baek...

91
00:04:39,964 --> 00:04:41,615
and our company were nearly put
in serious jeopardy.

92
00:04:42,149 --> 00:04:44,050
Then the person who caused all of that...

93
00:04:44,070 --> 00:04:45,619
suddenly joined our company...

94
00:04:46,119 --> 00:04:48,188
and chose a cliff
as the first shooting location.

95
00:04:48,555 --> 00:04:50,223
As the vice president, how could I
not be concerned?

96
00:04:50,690 --> 00:04:54,261
So you pushed me off the cliff?

97
00:04:57,531 --> 00:04:58,431
Listen.

98
00:04:58,591 --> 00:04:59,432
I did not...

99
00:05:00,173 --> 00:05:01,968
push you off that cliff.

100
00:05:06,484 --> 00:05:08,175
There is clear evidence right here.

101
00:05:08,351 --> 00:05:09,284
I already told you.

102
00:05:09,285 --> 00:05:12,112
The wind was so strong that I only went
that far before turning back.

103
00:05:14,664 --> 00:05:15,649
And...

104
00:05:16,349 --> 00:05:17,584
this cannot be considered evidence.

105
00:05:18,385 --> 00:05:20,687
It doesn't show anyone
pushing you off the cliff.

106
00:05:24,691 --> 00:05:25,725
I can go now, right?

107
00:05:39,606 --> 00:05:42,142
If someone really did
push you off that cliff,

108
00:05:43,302 --> 00:05:46,046
do you think that person would stop there?

109
00:05:46,713 --> 00:05:49,516
What do you mean?

110
00:05:49,938 --> 00:05:50,658
Wouldn't they...

111
00:05:51,952 --> 00:05:53,987
try to come after you again?

112
00:05:56,223 --> 00:05:59,692
They have not achieved their goal yet.

113
00:06:02,062 --> 00:06:03,163
So...

114
00:06:04,100 --> 00:06:05,298
stop making a scene...

115
00:06:08,322 --> 00:06:09,475
and watch your back.

116
00:06:29,990 --> 00:06:32,058
All you need is the company seal here.

117
00:06:32,392 --> 00:06:34,805
Our Vice President has the company seal,

118
00:06:34,832 --> 00:06:36,832
but he is out of the office right now.

119
00:06:36,845 --> 00:06:37,764
Oh, really?

120
00:06:38,479 --> 00:06:40,667
Do I have to come back again
just for this?

121
00:06:42,065 --> 00:06:44,371
Please wait here for a minute.

122
00:06:55,248 --> 00:06:56,357
Come on.

123
00:07:12,788 --> 00:07:15,235
I knew I was a genius.

124
00:07:15,481 --> 00:07:16,501
All right.

125
00:07:23,633 --> 00:07:24,611
Okay.

126
00:07:34,410 --> 00:07:35,355
Ms. Song.

127
00:07:35,624 --> 00:07:36,356
Yes?

128
00:07:36,357 --> 00:07:39,210
The client says he's short on time
and wants us to hurry.

129
00:07:39,230 --> 00:07:40,927
Okay. I'll be right down.

130
00:07:40,944 --> 00:07:41,928
All right.

131
00:07:48,742 --> 00:07:50,537
Something doesn't add up.

132
00:07:51,171 --> 00:07:53,573
The person who took the medicine suffered,

133
00:07:53,574 --> 00:07:56,176
while the one who gave it to her
did nothing wrong?

134
00:07:56,574 --> 00:07:59,245
Do you really think I would have given her
the medicine that could harm her?

135
00:07:59,294 --> 00:08:00,814
That is what makes this so strange.

136
00:08:00,815 --> 00:08:03,984
The medicine couldn't have
turned poisonous on its own.

137
00:08:04,173 --> 00:08:06,286
She's the one who's poisonous.

138
00:08:06,333 --> 00:08:07,900
She kept this bottled up for three years,

139
00:08:07,901 --> 00:08:10,690
and now she's firing it all at me
like poison darts...

140
00:08:10,760 --> 00:08:11,725
just to make me suffer.

141
00:08:11,833 --> 00:08:14,894
So you think your wife is doing this
just to make you suffer?

142
00:08:14,895 --> 00:08:17,564
Why else would she keep me in the dark
for three years?

143
00:08:17,600 --> 00:08:19,132
Who knows?

144
00:08:20,867 --> 00:08:22,235
It's not quite ready yet.

145
00:08:22,342 --> 00:08:23,054
What?

146
00:08:25,605 --> 00:08:27,605
Just say, hypothetically,

147
00:08:28,441 --> 00:08:30,571
what would you do if your wife was...

148
00:08:30,572 --> 00:08:31,578
telling the truth?

149
00:08:31,911 --> 00:08:33,680
What are you talking about?

150
00:08:33,681 --> 00:08:34,714
What if...

151
00:08:36,082 --> 00:08:37,037
you really are a murderer?

152
00:08:37,631 --> 00:08:39,858
What are you saying right now?

153
00:08:39,898 --> 00:08:42,144
I told you to control your temper.

154
00:08:42,145 --> 00:08:44,624
Sit down. You should hear me out
before you get angry.

155
00:08:49,662 --> 00:08:53,700
Calm down, and let's
think this through again.

156
00:08:54,300 --> 00:08:57,404
You gave your wife medicine
that you believed was completely safe.

157
00:08:57,568 --> 00:09:00,140
But what does your wife claim?

158
00:09:00,407 --> 00:09:02,708
She says the baby died
because of that medicine.

159
00:09:02,709 --> 00:09:03,632
Okay.

160
00:09:03,633 --> 00:09:04,677
Then let me ask you again.

161
00:09:04,853 --> 00:09:11,284
Is there any particular reason
you are so certain that you are innocent?

162
00:09:11,367 --> 00:09:12,526
How many times do I have to say this?

163
00:09:12,527 --> 00:09:15,313
I never gave my wife medicine
that could harm her,

164
00:09:15,314 --> 00:09:16,747
and I had no reason to do so.

165
00:09:16,773 --> 00:09:19,426
But that's the thing about life.

166
00:09:19,500 --> 00:09:25,098
Things don't always go
according to our intentions or plans.

167
00:09:26,120 --> 00:09:30,170
Unexpected variables
and unforeseen accidents can arise.

168
00:09:30,359 --> 00:09:35,241
In fact, those things happen
more often than we think.

169
00:09:36,626 --> 00:09:37,577
So,

170
00:09:38,326 --> 00:09:42,582
you're saying I should
consider other possibilities too.

171
00:09:42,744 --> 00:09:44,484
Exactly.

172
00:09:46,812 --> 00:09:48,188
Even an ember you think is dead...

173
00:09:49,222 --> 00:09:51,491
may still be burning.

174
00:09:54,294 --> 00:09:56,229
- By the way, Counselor.
- Yes?

175
00:09:56,863 --> 00:09:59,999
I think you should put out
that fire first.

176
00:10:11,211 --> 00:10:12,545
It's so soggy.

177
00:10:17,917 --> 00:10:21,554
Did that really happen because of
the medicine your husband gave you?

178
00:10:21,888 --> 00:10:23,022
But...

179
00:10:24,457 --> 00:10:26,493
my husband insists
it had nothing to do with him.

180
00:10:26,759 --> 00:10:28,068
I don't really understand.

181
00:10:28,254 --> 00:10:30,029
Of course you don't.

182
00:10:30,930 --> 00:10:32,365
My husband and I...

183
00:10:33,500 --> 00:10:34,934
make no sense anyway.

184
00:10:36,605 --> 00:10:38,304
At work,

185
00:10:38,925 --> 00:10:40,607
we are business partners
who cooperate with each other.

186
00:10:41,574 --> 00:10:42,809
Outside of work,

187
00:10:43,443 --> 00:10:45,044
we are enemies
fighting through a divorce lawsuit.

188
00:10:48,515 --> 00:10:49,315
But...

189
00:10:50,049 --> 00:10:51,784
do you know what really hurts?

190
00:10:53,953 --> 00:10:54,988
My husband...

191
00:10:56,322 --> 00:10:57,991
has already put it all behind him.

192
00:10:59,425 --> 00:11:01,425
Whenever I try to talk about it,

193
00:11:02,328 --> 00:11:04,130
he gets angry first.

194
00:11:06,633 --> 00:11:08,701
He asks why I am still talking
about our dead child.

195
00:11:10,613 --> 00:11:11,617
He asks why...

196
00:11:14,541 --> 00:11:16,776
why my time is still frozen there.

197
00:11:20,313 --> 00:11:21,447
Every time he says that,

198
00:11:23,373 --> 00:11:25,679
it feels like he's blaming me.

199
00:11:28,217 --> 00:11:28,955
Whenever...

200
00:11:30,857 --> 00:11:32,525
I think about that day,

201
00:11:33,511 --> 00:11:35,511
it still feels like hell.

202
00:11:40,466 --> 00:11:41,467
It feels like...

203
00:11:43,309 --> 00:11:45,405
this hell will never end.

204
00:11:49,375 --> 00:11:50,710
But my husband is different.

205
00:11:53,102 --> 00:11:53,980
He is...

206
00:11:56,216 --> 00:11:57,617
completely different from me.

207
00:11:58,484 --> 00:12:01,955
He probably has not forgotten everything.

208
00:12:03,858 --> 00:12:04,924
To be honest,

209
00:12:05,505 --> 00:12:08,494
I still haven't cleared out
my child's room.

210
00:12:10,463 --> 00:12:13,099
It has been a year since his mother
took him and left home,

211
00:12:14,334 --> 00:12:15,602
but his room...

212
00:12:16,778 --> 00:12:18,104
is still exactly the way it was
a year ago.

213
00:12:19,825 --> 00:12:21,641
I felt like...

214
00:12:21,918 --> 00:12:22,976
I couldn't bear...

215
00:12:24,777 --> 00:12:26,012
the sense of loss otherwise.

216
00:12:31,423 --> 00:12:32,318
Are you okay?

217
00:12:37,190 --> 00:12:38,124
I'm sorry.

218
00:12:39,158 --> 00:12:40,293
I'm getting carried away.

219
00:12:53,873 --> 00:12:54,774
Won Ho.

220
00:12:58,478 --> 00:12:59,946
I will have a beer too.

221
00:13:00,990 --> 00:13:02,015
Thank you.

222
00:13:04,083 --> 00:13:06,219
Why didn't you call?
Drinking all by yourself?

223
00:13:06,990 --> 00:13:08,297
Kyung Tae.

224
00:13:09,055 --> 00:13:10,290
For some reason,

225
00:13:11,988 --> 00:13:14,297
I feel like this whole thing might just
remain an unsolved mystery.

226
00:13:15,128 --> 00:13:16,141
An unsolved mystery?

227
00:13:17,021 --> 00:13:18,631
I went to the clinic today.

228
00:13:20,867 --> 00:13:24,370
I wanted to find out if there really had
been something wrong with it back then.

229
00:13:25,505 --> 00:13:26,406
So?

230
00:13:27,293 --> 00:13:29,319
Did you find anything out?

231
00:13:31,110 --> 00:13:33,546
Just as I thought, there was
nothing wrong with the medicine.

232
00:13:34,013 --> 00:13:36,649
And there's no way
it could have caused the miscarriage.

233
00:13:38,851 --> 00:13:40,253
Then what really happened?

234
00:13:41,921 --> 00:13:45,024
Mi Young is not the type to make
something like that up for no reason.

235
00:13:45,595 --> 00:13:47,760
She just can't let it go.

236
00:13:48,594 --> 00:13:49,429
Unresolved feelings?

237
00:13:49,948 --> 00:13:52,906
I think she wants to blame me
for everything...

238
00:13:52,907 --> 00:13:55,101
that happened around the time
we lost the baby.

239
00:13:56,229 --> 00:13:58,438
The volunteer work with Mr. Kwon,

240
00:13:59,369 --> 00:14:00,573
the medicine, everything.

241
00:14:01,007 --> 00:14:03,076
That's a bit unfair, though.

242
00:14:03,409 --> 00:14:05,611
She wouldn't be able
to live with herself...

243
00:14:06,516 --> 00:14:08,281
if she believed it was all her fault.

244
00:14:13,019 --> 00:14:14,754
Mi Young wanted Dal Rae to be born...

245
00:14:15,129 --> 00:14:16,989
more desperately than anything.

246
00:14:17,867 --> 00:14:19,592
You wanted her just as badly.

247
00:14:20,793 --> 00:14:21,894
You both wanted that.

248
00:14:29,408 --> 00:14:30,436
But...

249
00:14:31,304 --> 00:14:32,635
if you just leave things like this,

250
00:14:33,429 --> 00:14:34,974
won't that put you
in a difficult position?

251
00:14:36,042 --> 00:14:39,645
Mi Young will keep blaming you
all the way through the trial.

252
00:14:40,847 --> 00:14:42,415
I don't care about that.

253
00:14:44,889 --> 00:14:46,719
The problem is that
she is the one suffering more.

254
00:15:01,100 --> 00:15:04,637
Why is it so suffocating in here?

255
00:15:04,997 --> 00:15:06,839
Is it the sweet potatoes?

256
00:15:07,774 --> 00:15:08,741
No.

257
00:15:09,542 --> 00:15:11,144
The sweet potatoes have
nothing to do with it.

258
00:15:11,952 --> 00:15:13,846
It's suffocating
because this place is packed.

259
00:15:14,752 --> 00:15:15,882
Thanks to a certain someone.

260
00:15:18,985 --> 00:15:20,787
Oh, Mr. Ji is here.

261
00:15:24,205 --> 00:15:26,171
Why are you so late?

262
00:15:26,172 --> 00:15:27,326
I've been waiting for you.

263
00:15:27,391 --> 00:15:29,128
Why are you coming out of there?

264
00:15:31,205 --> 00:15:32,031
Take her.

265
00:15:34,677 --> 00:15:35,668
Come on.

266
00:15:40,106 --> 00:15:42,141
You said Kyung Tae pushed you
off the cliff?

267
00:15:42,224 --> 00:15:43,342
Yes.

268
00:15:43,590 --> 00:15:46,612
The guy who is always glued to your side.

269
00:15:46,748 --> 00:15:49,048
I met him in person today
and asked him about it.

270
00:15:49,582 --> 00:15:50,516
And what did he say?

271
00:15:50,555 --> 00:15:51,584
Did he admit it?

272
00:15:51,635 --> 00:15:53,635
Of course he denied it.

273
00:15:53,853 --> 00:15:56,122
But he threatened me.

274
00:15:56,160 --> 00:15:56,756
What?

275
00:15:56,893 --> 00:15:59,706
He told me to stop making scenes
and watch my back.

276
00:15:59,806 --> 00:16:02,500
That doesn't sound like a threat.
Sounds more like advice.

277
00:16:02,655 --> 00:16:03,320
What?

278
00:16:03,353 --> 00:16:06,065
Enough. Kyung Tae would never do that.

279
00:16:06,153 --> 00:16:08,568
I'm telling you, it's him.

280
00:16:08,586 --> 00:16:09,502
Come on.

281
00:16:09,646 --> 00:16:12,672
By the way, did you tell him...

282
00:16:13,172 --> 00:16:15,041
that I took those scandal photos?

283
00:16:15,638 --> 00:16:16,776
Scandal photos?

284
00:16:16,851 --> 00:16:18,277
You know,

285
00:16:18,398 --> 00:16:20,398
the photos I took and showed you.

286
00:16:20,971 --> 00:16:24,450
The ones that appeared in the scandal
article about Calvin and your wife.

287
00:16:24,678 --> 00:16:25,985
He said,

288
00:16:26,244 --> 00:16:27,720
"Do you have any idea
how much trouble you caused..."

289
00:16:27,871 --> 00:16:30,656
"the people at our company
by taking those photos?"

290
00:16:31,023 --> 00:16:33,878
That's strange.
Kyung Tae shouldn't know about that.

291
00:16:34,160 --> 00:16:36,028
See? I told you he was suspicious.

292
00:16:36,131 --> 00:16:38,464
Fine. You're right about everything.

293
00:16:38,472 --> 00:16:40,472
Now go. I'm tired.

294
00:16:40,473 --> 00:16:41,400
Go on.

295
00:16:42,034 --> 00:16:44,034
I don't want to. I'm sleeping here.

296
00:16:44,496 --> 00:16:45,252
What?

297
00:16:45,359 --> 00:16:47,473
I told you I was threatened.

298
00:16:47,843 --> 00:16:49,909
I'm terrified.
There's no way I'm sleeping alone.

299
00:16:57,884 --> 00:16:58,985
Then let's do this.

300
00:16:59,644 --> 00:17:02,255
My brother and my mother
come in and out of here sometimes,

301
00:17:02,622 --> 00:17:03,656
so let's go to your room.

302
00:17:05,525 --> 00:17:06,392
Really?

303
00:17:06,484 --> 00:17:09,428
Since you're so scared,
I guess I'll stay with you tonight.

304
00:17:10,404 --> 00:17:12,798
Then should we go to my room
and order some chicken?

305
00:17:12,799 --> 00:17:14,166
Sure. Have fun.

306
00:17:16,284 --> 00:17:17,236
What?

307
00:17:17,770 --> 00:17:19,772
You can't do this!

308
00:17:19,773 --> 00:17:21,407
Open the door!

309
00:17:21,580 --> 00:17:24,210
Stop messing around.
Lock your door and go to sleep.

310
00:17:25,100 --> 00:17:27,480
I'm really scared to be alone!

311
00:17:44,564 --> 00:17:47,733
Was our Princess Dal Rae scared?

312
00:17:47,970 --> 00:17:51,070
Don't worry. Daddy is right here with you.

313
00:17:51,890 --> 00:17:56,108
Daddy will protect both of his princesses.
Kiss, kiss.

314
00:18:32,974 --> 00:18:36,082
I'm sure it's that brooch.

315
00:18:36,849 --> 00:18:39,318
This is so pretty.

316
00:18:40,152 --> 00:18:42,187
Won Ho is so sweet.

317
00:18:42,188 --> 00:18:44,490
He even bought you something like this
as a pregnancy gift.

318
00:18:44,671 --> 00:18:47,529
He picked it up on his business trip
to Milan, thinking of me.

319
00:18:47,530 --> 00:18:50,563
That's enough. You're making me jealous.

320
00:18:50,716 --> 00:18:52,798
That's exactly what I was trying to do.

321
00:18:55,223 --> 00:18:56,535
Come on.

322
00:18:57,169 --> 00:18:59,705
Why is the brooch Mi Young lost...

323
00:19:00,238 --> 00:19:02,508
inside Mr. Kang's drawer?

324
00:19:14,120 --> 00:19:15,021
Mr. Kang?

325
00:19:16,025 --> 00:19:16,718
Yes?

326
00:19:17,123 --> 00:19:18,758
I need to talk to you for a moment.

327
00:19:24,597 --> 00:19:25,665
Say that again.

328
00:19:26,132 --> 00:19:27,833
What did you just say to me?

329
00:19:28,010 --> 00:19:31,003
I told you I would agree to whatever
you want in the property settlement.

330
00:19:31,043 --> 00:19:32,772
No. Not that. What did you say after that?

331
00:19:33,039 --> 00:19:35,039
In exchange for agreeing
to the property settlement, what?

332
00:19:35,474 --> 00:19:37,209
You want me to never bring up
the medicine again?

333
00:19:37,334 --> 00:19:39,045
And when we go to court,
I want you to drop...

334
00:19:39,412 --> 00:19:42,014
anything about the miscarriage
and focus on the other issues.

335
00:19:42,061 --> 00:19:43,315
Why should I do that?

336
00:19:43,441 --> 00:19:45,451
You already have plenty
of other grudges against me.

337
00:19:45,794 --> 00:19:47,920
Why bring up something so sensitive
on top of all that?

338
00:19:48,354 --> 00:19:51,323
We're getting divorced anyway, so let's
just settle things as amicably as we can.

339
00:19:51,857 --> 00:19:53,659
And it's not like
you have anything to lose.

340
00:19:53,841 --> 00:19:56,062
You could walk away with a lot more
just by keeping your mouth shut.

341
00:20:00,533 --> 00:20:01,667
Ms. Song.

342
00:20:02,212 --> 00:20:05,538
Are you accusing me of stealing?

343
00:20:06,272 --> 00:20:09,139
It wasn't like I did it on purpose.

344
00:20:10,976 --> 00:20:13,612
I happened to see inside your drawer,

345
00:20:14,246 --> 00:20:17,516
while I was looking for the company seal.

346
00:20:18,050 --> 00:20:19,118
And,

347
00:20:19,877 --> 00:20:23,956
there was a brooch in there
that Mrs. Baek had lost years ago.

348
00:20:24,177 --> 00:20:27,193
The pin that mysteriously
disappeared overnight,

349
00:20:27,330 --> 00:20:30,129
- just happened to be...
- You happened to see inside my drawer?

350
00:20:30,950 --> 00:20:33,466
It's locked. How could you
have just happened to see it?

351
00:20:33,490 --> 00:20:35,201
I told you.

352
00:20:35,364 --> 00:20:38,771
I had no choice because I was looking
for the company seal.

353
00:20:41,506 --> 00:20:44,110
Fine. I found the key and unlocked it.

354
00:20:44,208 --> 00:20:46,345
So the person who broke
into someone else's drawer...

355
00:20:47,346 --> 00:20:48,922
is accusing me of being a thief?

356
00:20:48,968 --> 00:20:52,995
I swear I only opened it
to find the company seal.

357
00:20:53,020 --> 00:20:55,855
Even so, how can you
just touch someone else's belongings?

358
00:20:56,859 --> 00:20:58,023
Apologize.

359
00:20:58,024 --> 00:21:00,926
I wasn't snooping around your things.

360
00:21:02,144 --> 00:21:03,831
And why are you getting angry?

361
00:21:03,832 --> 00:21:05,832
Do you think I won't get mad...

362
00:21:06,232 --> 00:21:07,500
when you're framing me?

363
00:21:07,544 --> 00:21:09,976
I was just asking.

364
00:21:09,977 --> 00:21:12,371
You weren't just asking.

365
00:21:13,139 --> 00:21:14,406
Apologize properly.

366
00:21:16,442 --> 00:21:17,309
Sorry.

367
00:21:17,310 --> 00:21:18,811
Is that supposed to be an apology?

368
00:21:18,864 --> 00:21:20,646
I just did.

369
00:21:20,662 --> 00:21:21,946
Are you talking down to me?

370
00:21:22,041 --> 00:21:24,948
Why does formal or informal speech matter?
I apologized anyway.

371
00:21:24,949 --> 00:21:25,985
Easily?

372
00:21:26,022 --> 00:21:30,055
If I were going to settle things easily,
do you think we'd have ended up in court?

373
00:21:30,873 --> 00:21:32,873
Then are you really determined
to take this all the way?

374
00:21:33,173 --> 00:21:36,829
Who was it that tried to silence me first
by dangling a property settlement?

375
00:21:38,680 --> 00:21:41,046
So, are you going to spend your
whole life thinking about Dal Rae?

376
00:21:41,400 --> 00:21:43,302
How could you possibly understand me...

377
00:21:44,603 --> 00:21:46,172
When you completely forgot about Dal Rae.

378
00:21:47,039 --> 00:21:47,773
What?

379
00:21:48,340 --> 00:21:50,776
You never even held Dal Rae,

380
00:21:51,477 --> 00:21:53,212
so she meant nothing to you.

381
00:21:53,372 --> 00:21:54,246
And you?

382
00:21:55,548 --> 00:21:56,582
Did you?

383
00:21:58,484 --> 00:22:02,121
You've been doing this for years
over a baby you never even gave birth to.

384
00:22:02,822 --> 00:22:04,510
That's taking things too far.

385
00:22:05,177 --> 00:22:06,125
Too far?

386
00:22:07,293 --> 00:22:08,027
How...

387
00:22:09,401 --> 00:22:10,851
How could you...

388
00:22:11,597 --> 00:22:14,224
So just let it go now.

389
00:22:18,504 --> 00:22:20,077
Don't you think so?

390
00:22:20,284 --> 00:22:22,474
It's time to let it go.

391
00:22:24,417 --> 00:22:25,377
Mi Young.

392
00:22:27,813 --> 00:22:28,848
Are you okay?

393
00:22:32,740 --> 00:22:34,519
Why are you showing up
unannounced like this?

394
00:22:34,626 --> 00:22:35,988
Does this happen a lot?

395
00:22:36,488 --> 00:22:37,213
What?

396
00:22:37,346 --> 00:22:39,091
Mi Young is crying like that,

397
00:22:39,497 --> 00:22:41,117
and you don't look
the least bit concerned.

398
00:22:41,153 --> 00:22:42,962
I asked you why you're here again.

399
00:22:43,360 --> 00:22:46,365
Fire Mi Young.

400
00:22:47,166 --> 00:22:47,967
Fire?

401
00:22:48,180 --> 00:22:50,469
I can't have her by your side anymore.

402
00:22:51,136 --> 00:22:54,106
Not as your business partner,
and not as your wife either.

403
00:22:55,685 --> 00:22:58,811
Though, of course,
the marriage will be over soon anyway.

404
00:23:00,569 --> 00:23:01,313
No.

405
00:23:02,781 --> 00:23:04,083
I can't fire her.

406
00:23:06,042 --> 00:23:08,354
You're really pushing it lately.

407
00:23:09,755 --> 00:23:11,390
Is crossing the line your hobby?

408
00:23:11,687 --> 00:23:13,687
Do you think I'm a pushover?

409
00:23:13,967 --> 00:23:15,060
Do you?

410
00:23:16,028 --> 00:23:16,896
And what about you?

411
00:23:17,396 --> 00:23:19,396
You said you'd make Mi Young happy,

412
00:23:20,340 --> 00:23:22,568
but all you do is
make her cry like this every day.

413
00:23:23,769 --> 00:23:26,205
How would you know
whether she cries or laughs every day?

414
00:23:27,907 --> 00:23:29,141
She cried yesterday too.

415
00:23:29,732 --> 00:23:30,743
Because of you.

416
00:23:32,912 --> 00:23:33,946
Do you get it now?

417
00:23:34,780 --> 00:23:38,717
Mi Young can only be unhappy
as long as she's by your side.

418
00:23:56,545 --> 00:23:57,736
Thank you, as always.

419
00:23:57,737 --> 00:23:59,305
You're welcome.

420
00:24:01,024 --> 00:24:05,544
By the way, how is
my brother and his wife's lawsuit going?

421
00:24:05,664 --> 00:24:08,514
It's taking longer than I expected,

422
00:24:09,248 --> 00:24:11,850
but we're currently waiting
for the second family investigation.

423
00:24:12,017 --> 00:24:13,185
A family investigation?

424
00:24:13,786 --> 00:24:15,020
That's important.

425
00:24:15,170 --> 00:24:16,588
How do you know so much about it?

426
00:24:16,743 --> 00:24:19,988
Actually, I have some experience.

427
00:24:20,154 --> 00:24:21,260
I'm divorced.

428
00:24:21,401 --> 00:24:23,121
It's been five years this year.

429
00:24:23,562 --> 00:24:25,421
Actually, I'm divorced too.

430
00:24:26,065 --> 00:24:27,866
I'm only...

431
00:24:29,508 --> 00:24:30,402
a year into it.

432
00:24:30,714 --> 00:24:31,588
Really?

433
00:24:32,304 --> 00:24:33,439
Why are you so surprised?

434
00:24:33,548 --> 00:24:37,001
Whoever he is,
he must be crazy to lose you.

435
00:24:37,876 --> 00:24:39,278
Someone this lovable...

436
00:24:43,410 --> 00:24:44,516
Duck down.

437
00:24:45,250 --> 00:24:46,518
Hurry.

438
00:24:50,889 --> 00:24:54,960
Where did he go off to this time?

439
00:24:55,130 --> 00:24:57,629
Is he grilling on the rooftop again?

440
00:24:57,790 --> 00:24:59,398
That fatso...

441
00:25:20,465 --> 00:25:22,755
Is this really the best
you can do, An Hee Ju?

442
00:25:23,228 --> 00:25:23,959
Excuse me?

443
00:25:24,039 --> 00:25:27,559
Look at the difference in brightness
between these two faces.

444
00:25:28,027 --> 00:25:30,763
The bride's face is completely
washed out, and the groom...

445
00:25:31,797 --> 00:25:34,299
Why am I having to tell
the photographer this?

446
00:25:34,986 --> 00:25:37,899
Connections or not,
this is completely unprofessional.

447
00:25:38,570 --> 00:25:40,706
Fix this properly and bring it back.

448
00:25:50,249 --> 00:25:51,116
What's going on?

449
00:25:51,526 --> 00:25:53,351
Seriously, they might end up fighting.

450
00:25:58,824 --> 00:25:59,858
Won Ho.

451
00:25:59,960 --> 00:26:01,126
Where are you going?

452
00:26:03,262 --> 00:26:05,431
Where is he going at this hour?

453
00:26:05,764 --> 00:26:06,932
Hey.

454
00:26:09,481 --> 00:26:10,930
What are you trying to do right now?

455
00:26:11,037 --> 00:26:13,123
I'm just giving you work.

456
00:26:13,929 --> 00:26:15,407
Do you think I'll give up,

457
00:26:15,874 --> 00:26:17,276
just because you're doing this?

458
00:26:17,976 --> 00:26:20,979
No, I'm going to find out the truth.

459
00:26:21,280 --> 00:26:24,802
That you're the one who tried
to push me off the cliff.

460
00:26:25,193 --> 00:26:26,573
But I think you're running out of time.

461
00:26:26,985 --> 00:26:27,886
What?

462
00:26:28,087 --> 00:26:31,356
Go and finish today's work
before the day is over.

463
00:26:36,995 --> 00:26:38,995
He's driving me crazy!

464
00:26:39,238 --> 00:26:40,732
What am I supposed to do with him?

465
00:26:45,704 --> 00:26:46,972
The cliff?

466
00:26:51,310 --> 00:26:53,479
Are you still feeling that way?

467
00:26:54,833 --> 00:26:55,681
Sorry?

468
00:26:56,148 --> 00:26:57,249
Feeling what?

469
00:26:57,850 --> 00:27:00,185
Are you still having a hard time?

470
00:27:07,047 --> 00:27:09,047
Take all the time you need.

471
00:27:48,500 --> 00:27:50,302
- Take care of things.
- Okay.

472
00:27:52,905 --> 00:27:54,273
Already clocking out?

473
00:27:54,645 --> 00:27:57,609
I'm not feeling well today,
so I'm going to leave early.

474
00:27:57,965 --> 00:27:59,845
Could you finish up for me?

475
00:27:59,985 --> 00:28:02,145
Sure. Go get some rest.

476
00:28:02,587 --> 00:28:03,482
Thanks.

477
00:28:04,516 --> 00:28:05,651
Mi Young.

478
00:28:08,654 --> 00:28:12,024
Do you remember that brooch?

479
00:28:12,558 --> 00:28:15,494
The one you lost years ago
when you were out on business.

480
00:28:15,994 --> 00:28:17,496
Did you ever find it?

481
00:28:17,803 --> 00:28:19,997
No, I didn't.

482
00:28:20,759 --> 00:28:23,094
Why are you suddenly asking about that?

483
00:28:24,769 --> 00:28:25,809
Well...

484
00:28:26,055 --> 00:28:28,874
Just popped into my head.

485
00:28:30,809 --> 00:28:32,565
- I'm leaving.
- Okay.

486
00:28:37,903 --> 00:28:39,551
I'm pretty sure...

487
00:28:40,211 --> 00:28:42,486
it's the same brooch.

488
00:29:00,044 --> 00:29:01,546
Are you okay?

489
00:29:06,111 --> 00:29:08,480
Did you get shaken up earlier?

490
00:29:08,780 --> 00:29:11,300
No. I was just worried about you.

491
00:29:12,560 --> 00:29:15,354
Seeing you cry earlier really worried me.

492
00:29:16,855 --> 00:29:19,358
I'm okay now.
You don't have to worry about me.

493
00:29:19,885 --> 00:29:22,854
And why did you come
to our company earlier?

494
00:29:35,729 --> 00:29:36,608
Oh, my.

495
00:29:43,181 --> 00:29:46,818
I'm thinking about setting up
a wedding-related subsidiary this time.

496
00:29:47,140 --> 00:29:49,221
A total wedding company, like J&WHITE.

497
00:29:50,686 --> 00:29:51,823
That's great.

498
00:29:52,157 --> 00:29:55,727
You already have all the infrastructure
for wedding halls.

499
00:29:56,273 --> 00:29:58,830
A Calvin-affiliated wedding company...

500
00:29:59,339 --> 00:30:00,666
That's such a great idea.

501
00:30:01,383 --> 00:30:02,868
I've been thinking a lot.

502
00:30:03,461 --> 00:30:07,765
I know how much passion and responsibility
you have for J&WHITE.

503
00:30:09,874 --> 00:30:13,078
And now I can finally
make the proposal with confidence.

504
00:30:14,846 --> 00:30:17,282
I'd like you to take
on the position of CEO...

505
00:30:18,784 --> 00:30:19,894
of the new Calvin Wedding.

506
00:30:57,892 --> 00:30:59,257
Dal Rae, how have you been?

507
00:31:00,859 --> 00:31:01,993
You're not cold, are you?

508
00:31:06,064 --> 00:31:08,789
You haven't forgotten
your dad already, have you?

509
00:31:12,437 --> 00:31:15,173
Time really flies, doesn't it?

510
00:31:17,676 --> 00:31:19,911
It's already been three years,

511
00:31:22,214 --> 00:31:23,815
since I had to say goodbye to you.

512
00:32:03,118 --> 00:32:08,118
(Cremains Reception Room)

513
00:32:15,717 --> 00:32:16,735
Oh, no.

514
00:32:27,746 --> 00:32:29,548
Just a moment.

515
00:32:29,549 --> 00:32:31,950
Let me think about it one more time.

516
00:32:32,384 --> 00:32:34,686
I think it'll be too hot for my baby.

517
00:32:36,677 --> 00:32:39,191
I'm sorry.

518
00:34:15,707 --> 00:34:17,707
People probably don't know...

519
00:34:18,727 --> 00:34:22,260
how beautiful this place is
when the warm spring comes.

520
00:34:24,180 --> 00:34:27,799
And they don't know how much I miss you.

521
00:34:29,901 --> 00:34:31,269
How much I long to see you again.

522
00:34:35,740 --> 00:34:37,075
But it doesn't matter to me at all.

523
00:34:40,745 --> 00:34:42,113
My Dal Rae.

524
00:34:45,584 --> 00:34:47,953
As long as you know,
that's all that matters.

525
00:35:02,507 --> 00:35:04,970
Where is he? Today is so important.

526
00:35:10,108 --> 00:35:11,242
Seriously?

527
00:35:11,543 --> 00:35:14,312
Is Mr. Ji not answering his phone?

528
00:35:14,452 --> 00:35:17,616
He was absent without notice yesterday,
and now he's disappeared.

529
00:35:19,217 --> 00:35:22,654
He absolutely has to be there today.
It's the day of the home evaluation.

530
00:35:25,033 --> 00:35:26,424
I see.

531
00:35:28,393 --> 00:35:29,894
Why are you looking at me like that?

532
00:35:30,328 --> 00:35:31,765
Are you worried I stole something again?

533
00:35:31,790 --> 00:35:33,790
No way.

534
00:35:37,702 --> 00:35:38,937
What's this?

535
00:35:42,203 --> 00:35:44,843
That's why I answered your call just now.

536
00:35:45,163 --> 00:35:49,514
I ignored everyone else's calls.
You're the only exception, as my lawyer.

537
00:35:49,650 --> 00:35:51,828
I guess I should be so honored,

538
00:35:51,852 --> 00:35:54,085
that I ought to bow down to you.

539
00:35:54,294 --> 00:35:55,654
I'm serious.

540
00:35:55,721 --> 00:35:58,523
Exactly. What's gotten into you?

541
00:35:58,923 --> 00:36:01,634
You should be doing everything you can
to win over the investigator,

542
00:36:01,635 --> 00:36:03,662
and you're leisurely out there fishing?

543
00:36:03,861 --> 00:36:05,861
It just worked out that way.

544
00:36:06,149 --> 00:36:07,465
You need to go right now.

545
00:36:07,829 --> 00:36:10,535
The family investigation starts at 2 p.m.

546
00:36:10,715 --> 00:36:12,748
Even if you're late,
get over there right now.

547
00:36:13,905 --> 00:36:14,973
I'm not going.

548
00:36:15,340 --> 00:36:17,242
It'll only make things
harder for both of us.

549
00:36:17,976 --> 00:36:21,046
It's better if we don't
run into each other today.

550
00:36:21,226 --> 00:36:23,481
What exactly is so special about today?

551
00:36:32,824 --> 00:36:35,360
Since your husband is absent,

552
00:36:35,660 --> 00:36:37,829
it'll be difficult to proceed today.

553
00:36:39,130 --> 00:36:39,964
I see.

554
00:36:41,066 --> 00:36:43,802
Then let's call it a day,

555
00:36:43,989 --> 00:36:46,371
and reschedule.

556
00:36:50,608 --> 00:36:53,678
I hated being alone so much.

557
00:36:55,146 --> 00:36:55,980
Sorry?

558
00:36:58,650 --> 00:37:00,785
I felt like I'd been thrown out,

559
00:37:01,892 --> 00:37:03,555
into this vast, cold world all by myself.

560
00:37:07,625 --> 00:37:08,593
It was...

561
00:37:10,328 --> 00:37:12,397
so frightening.

562
00:37:16,568 --> 00:37:20,071
My parents were my only family.

563
00:37:20,578 --> 00:37:22,578
I lost them all at once in an accident.

564
00:37:24,743 --> 00:37:26,845
Overnight, I became an orphan,

565
00:37:27,946 --> 00:37:28,880
and then,

566
00:37:30,812 --> 00:37:32,812
I suffered another devastating heartbreak.

567
00:37:53,964 --> 00:37:55,240
For a long time,

568
00:37:56,144 --> 00:37:58,643
my heart had been tightly closed
because of those wounds.

569
00:38:00,478 --> 00:38:02,277
The one who opened it again was...

570
00:38:05,784 --> 00:38:07,385
my husband.

571
00:38:09,154 --> 00:38:10,188
And then,

572
00:38:15,254 --> 00:38:17,328
a baby came into my life like a miracle.

573
00:38:19,007 --> 00:38:21,065
When I became pregnant,

574
00:38:23,034 --> 00:38:25,370
I felt like I'd been reborn.

575
00:38:27,605 --> 00:38:29,374
Because for that baby,

576
00:38:30,725 --> 00:38:33,878
there was nothing in this world
I was afraid of.

577
00:38:35,713 --> 00:38:37,081
I would've even gladly...

578
00:38:39,951 --> 00:38:42,053
died for her.

579
00:38:44,923 --> 00:38:46,558
As a mother,

580
00:38:48,003 --> 00:38:48,927
I thought...

581
00:38:52,330 --> 00:38:54,732
I could do anything.

582
00:38:57,268 --> 00:38:58,336
But...

583
00:39:01,674 --> 00:39:03,141
But, Investigator,

584
00:39:05,009 --> 00:39:06,044
where do you think...

585
00:39:08,646 --> 00:39:10,481
that baby is now?

586
00:39:14,752 --> 00:39:16,421
After I die...

587
00:39:18,122 --> 00:39:18,957
Or,

588
00:39:21,926 --> 00:39:23,695
even in my next life...

589
00:39:25,950 --> 00:39:27,899
Do you think I'll be
able to see the baby again?

590
00:39:39,644 --> 00:39:40,945
Hello.

591
00:39:41,279 --> 00:39:42,559
Hi, welcome.

592
00:39:47,585 --> 00:39:49,153
How have you been?

593
00:39:50,088 --> 00:39:51,589
Wait, who is this?

594
00:39:52,716 --> 00:39:54,259
Jeon Ji Hyun.

595
00:39:54,759 --> 00:39:57,228
No, you're Attorney Jeon Chi Hyun, right?

596
00:39:58,229 --> 00:40:01,189
Oh, you remember my name?

597
00:40:02,166 --> 00:40:03,801
Of course I remember.

598
00:40:04,141 --> 00:40:05,028
Oh, wait.

599
00:40:05,427 --> 00:40:06,504
Let me clean up.

600
00:40:07,939 --> 00:40:09,040
Seriously.

601
00:40:14,879 --> 00:40:15,947
Please, have a seat.

602
00:40:18,199 --> 00:40:19,346
Oh, my.

603
00:40:19,506 --> 00:40:21,920
It's been so long.

604
00:40:22,320 --> 00:40:24,320
You sure were amazing back then.

605
00:40:24,546 --> 00:40:26,886
Even after I beat you down like that,

606
00:40:26,887 --> 00:40:29,294
you kept getting back up,
taking hit after hit after hit.

607
00:40:29,424 --> 00:40:31,424
And in the end, you even lost your office.

608
00:40:31,437 --> 00:40:33,326
Beaten? Who said I got beaten?

609
00:40:33,410 --> 00:40:37,101
If you say so.
Anyway, I didn't get beaten.

610
00:40:38,169 --> 00:40:40,705
I tried to let it slide where I could,

611
00:40:41,208 --> 00:40:42,640
but isn't this going a bit too far?

612
00:40:43,341 --> 00:40:44,455
Going a bit too far? What is?

613
00:40:44,781 --> 00:40:46,377
The second family court evaluation.

614
00:40:46,461 --> 00:40:48,234
- You're the one who scheduled it.
- Yes.

615
00:40:48,366 --> 00:40:50,715
Yet you no-showed
without any advance notice.

616
00:40:51,649 --> 00:40:53,785
My client went
through all that trouble for nothing.

617
00:40:53,846 --> 00:40:55,553
Hey, come on.

618
00:40:55,554 --> 00:40:58,056
Are you seriously here
to complain about that?

619
00:40:58,219 --> 00:40:58,923
Yes.

620
00:40:59,190 --> 00:41:01,092
No. Wait, well...

621
00:41:01,379 --> 00:41:03,515
Then why else would I come here?

622
00:41:03,599 --> 00:41:05,026
I bet you were curious,

623
00:41:05,027 --> 00:41:05,952
wondering what this is,

624
00:41:05,953 --> 00:41:08,192
wondering what exactly I have planned
up my sleeve.

625
00:41:08,206 --> 00:41:11,366
I'm sure you came
because you couldn't stand not knowing.

626
00:41:11,432 --> 00:41:12,203
No.

627
00:41:12,299 --> 00:41:15,707
Mountains are mountains,
and rivers are rivers.

628
00:41:17,442 --> 00:41:19,243
You know what my nickname is, right?

629
00:41:19,275 --> 00:41:20,044
I don't.

630
00:41:20,047 --> 00:41:24,515
There's just one thing
even a legendary monster can't beat.

631
00:41:25,450 --> 00:41:26,284
And what's that?

632
00:41:26,595 --> 00:41:27,408
A blockhead.

633
00:41:27,775 --> 00:41:28,353
Sorry?

634
00:41:28,562 --> 00:41:31,442
We didn't attend because my client is
a complete blockhead.

635
00:41:31,526 --> 00:41:33,974
And I'm every bit as pissed off
about it as you are.

636
00:41:35,615 --> 00:41:39,686
I was stabbed in the back just like you.

637
00:41:42,834 --> 00:41:45,236
A blockhead is a blockhead,

638
00:41:45,468 --> 00:41:48,178
and backstabbing is backstabbing.

639
00:41:53,297 --> 00:41:54,979
But seriously, I wonder where he went.

640
00:41:56,364 --> 00:41:59,614
Where could he have gone,
skipping even the family court evaluation?

641
00:41:59,698 --> 00:42:02,520
And why on earth did he go there?

642
00:42:02,677 --> 00:42:04,077
What's that got to do with me?

643
00:42:04,190 --> 00:42:05,656
That's exactly your problem.

644
00:42:06,824 --> 00:42:08,892
A legendary monster
is a legendary monster,

645
00:42:08,976 --> 00:42:11,946
and Jeon Chi Hyun still has
a long way to go.

646
00:42:16,788 --> 00:42:17,635
Hey!

647
00:42:18,108 --> 00:42:18,936
Yes?

648
00:42:18,988 --> 00:42:21,172
Mr. Ji came in a moment ago.

649
00:42:21,288 --> 00:42:22,006
What?

650
00:42:22,055 --> 00:42:25,760
It looked like he'd been
to a fishing spot.

651
00:42:26,026 --> 00:42:27,311
A fishing spot?

652
00:42:38,423 --> 00:42:40,024
Did you go to the fishing spot?

653
00:42:41,012 --> 00:42:41,592
Yes.

654
00:42:42,727 --> 00:42:43,594
I see.

655
00:42:44,429 --> 00:42:47,532
Going to the family court evaluation
or not...

656
00:42:48,249 --> 00:42:49,642
is up to you.

657
00:42:58,709 --> 00:42:59,644
Oh, right.

658
00:43:00,216 --> 00:43:02,880
Calvin offered me...

659
00:43:03,781 --> 00:43:06,250
the director position at a new business.

660
00:43:09,430 --> 00:43:11,622
Calvin's starting a wedding business...

661
00:43:12,590 --> 00:43:13,891
and asked me to help.

662
00:43:17,028 --> 00:43:18,629
Okay. That's good.

663
00:43:19,697 --> 00:43:22,868
Then I guess once the trial's over,
everything will be settled.

664
00:43:26,855 --> 00:43:28,464
It's almost over.

665
00:43:28,548 --> 00:43:31,042
So let's not hurt each other anymore...

666
00:43:31,452 --> 00:43:32,443
and end it well.

667
00:43:33,244 --> 00:43:34,445
All I want now is...

668
00:43:35,819 --> 00:43:37,020
just that.

669
00:43:49,393 --> 00:43:51,097
Why do you think he went
to the fishing spot?

670
00:43:51,910 --> 00:43:52,563
Sorry?

671
00:43:52,750 --> 00:43:55,066
He even skipped
the family court evaluation.

672
00:43:55,150 --> 00:43:58,018
Of all places, why did he go
to a fishing spot?

673
00:44:00,938 --> 00:44:02,573
To just give up on everything...

674
00:44:03,230 --> 00:44:04,675
and clear his head?

675
00:44:07,232 --> 00:44:08,713
No, that's not it.

676
00:44:10,815 --> 00:44:13,951
There's no way the legendary monster
would have said that for no reason.

677
00:44:24,087 --> 00:44:24,962
Ms. Jeon...

678
00:44:26,164 --> 00:44:29,100
Today's the 22nd, right?

679
00:44:30,334 --> 00:44:31,102
Yes.

680
00:44:32,336 --> 00:44:33,204
What about it?

681
00:44:41,003 --> 00:44:43,314
- First, lock in the shoot schedule,
- Okay.

682
00:44:43,398 --> 00:44:48,102
and regarding the concept,
contact the studio and let me know.

683
00:45:13,032 --> 00:45:14,772
(Fishing spot)

684
00:46:01,648 --> 00:46:02,827
Are you here to fish?

685
00:46:03,302 --> 00:46:06,130
No, I'm just looking around.

686
00:46:06,142 --> 00:46:07,398
I see.

687
00:46:10,995 --> 00:46:13,430
Those just look
like bare branches, don't they?

688
00:46:13,745 --> 00:46:17,315
But they're not. Those are azalea trees.

689
00:46:18,426 --> 00:46:19,710
Azalea?

690
00:46:19,912 --> 00:46:24,448
When spring comes,
the azaleas here bloom so beautifully.

691
00:46:25,016 --> 00:46:27,218
I think it was about three years ago.

692
00:46:27,237 --> 00:46:30,321
A handsome young man came
and planted it there.

693
00:46:30,721 --> 00:46:34,558
I believe he said
his daughter's name was Dal Rae.

694
00:46:45,102 --> 00:46:47,605
From what I heard,
his story was very heartbreaking.

695
00:46:48,886 --> 00:46:52,310
Apparently the baby died
before it was even born.

696
00:46:57,748 --> 00:47:00,351
He brought the baby's ashes,
which weren't even a handful,

697
00:47:00,851 --> 00:47:03,020
and was begging me
to let him bury her there,

698
00:47:03,287 --> 00:47:05,823
looking utterly devastated.

699
00:47:07,158 --> 00:47:10,828
That's where he buried her?

700
00:47:11,289 --> 00:47:13,115
According to that young man,

701
00:47:13,437 --> 00:47:14,938
if the child had been born,

702
00:47:15,175 --> 00:47:18,169
she would have been born
when the azaleas bloomed.

703
00:47:20,953 --> 00:47:23,941
Did that young man...

704
00:47:25,009 --> 00:47:26,410
come today as well?

705
00:47:26,446 --> 00:47:28,446
Yes, he did.

706
00:47:29,246 --> 00:47:31,415
But it's really strange.

707
00:47:31,611 --> 00:47:34,652
He never comes
when the azaleas actually bloom.

708
00:47:35,105 --> 00:47:38,289
You have no idea
how beautiful those flowers are.

709
00:47:55,228 --> 00:47:58,183
Because of the official seal,
I had no choice.

710
00:47:58,267 --> 00:48:01,240
So that gives you the right to touch
other people's belongings?

711
00:48:01,533 --> 00:48:03,914
I wasn't trying to.

712
00:48:03,922 --> 00:48:05,253
Apologize!

713
00:48:08,328 --> 00:48:10,788
He didn't say anything about the brooch,

714
00:48:11,309 --> 00:48:14,024
but only got angry.

715
00:48:14,658 --> 00:48:16,394
Remember that brooch?

716
00:48:16,694 --> 00:48:18,229
Did you ever find it?

717
00:48:18,863 --> 00:48:20,998
No, I didn't.

718
00:48:21,699 --> 00:48:24,135
But why are you suddenly asking
about that?

719
00:48:24,535 --> 00:48:29,473
And Mi Young still hasn't found
that brooch yet.

720
00:48:30,161 --> 00:48:32,192
I'll get to the truth, no matter what.

721
00:48:32,366 --> 00:48:35,813
The person who tried to push me
off the cliff was you.

722
00:48:39,450 --> 00:48:42,253
And what was all that about?

723
00:48:43,387 --> 00:48:46,390
Gosh! This is giving me a headache!

724
00:49:14,752 --> 00:49:16,520
That was today.

725
00:49:17,087 --> 00:49:18,389
Time sure goes fast.

726
00:49:19,256 --> 00:49:21,625
Please pray hard for us.

727
00:49:22,226 --> 00:49:23,494
Don't worry about that.

728
00:49:24,161 --> 00:49:25,863
Why's your face so haggard?

729
00:49:27,264 --> 00:49:28,532
Have you eaten?

730
00:49:30,483 --> 00:49:31,402
This won't do.

731
00:49:31,869 --> 00:49:32,970
Let's go eat.

732
00:49:33,580 --> 00:49:34,605
Well...

733
00:49:35,940 --> 00:49:37,007
More than that,

734
00:49:37,975 --> 00:49:40,177
I want to talk to you some more.

735
00:49:40,711 --> 00:49:42,480
Can I make a confession?

736
00:49:45,516 --> 00:49:47,516
Today, it feels like...

737
00:49:49,378 --> 00:49:52,523
something's stuck here and won't go down.

738
00:49:53,224 --> 00:49:56,760
I feel like I'd feel a bit better
if I vent to you.

739
00:49:57,323 --> 00:49:59,029
Then go and wait for me inside.

740
00:49:59,030 --> 00:50:00,531
I'll prepare and come in later.

741
00:50:00,865 --> 00:50:01,765
Okay.

742
00:50:44,331 --> 00:50:45,543
I want to confess...

743
00:50:47,645 --> 00:50:49,179
my sins.

744
00:50:50,714 --> 00:50:51,582
Lord,

745
00:50:53,210 --> 00:50:54,311
today, I confess...

746
00:50:55,719 --> 00:50:57,154
my weakness...

747
00:50:59,523 --> 00:51:01,125
and my selfishness.

748
00:51:03,827 --> 00:51:04,728
All this time,

749
00:51:06,397 --> 00:51:07,665
through my selfishness,

750
00:51:08,999 --> 00:51:10,267
I endlessly...

751
00:51:11,502 --> 00:51:14,905
hurt my husband.

752
00:51:17,041 --> 00:51:20,811
I confess this past, and I repent.

753
00:51:23,205 --> 00:51:24,148
I...

754
00:51:27,551 --> 00:51:29,583
I thought I was the only one
who was struggling.

755
00:51:32,856 --> 00:51:34,358
That only I was in anguish,

756
00:51:35,626 --> 00:51:37,261
that only I deserved pity,

757
00:51:40,567 --> 00:51:42,666
and that only I was in pain.

758
00:51:46,873 --> 00:51:47,771
But...

759
00:51:50,007 --> 00:51:51,508
that was not the case.

760
00:51:53,611 --> 00:51:54,899
My husband was...

761
00:51:55,386 --> 00:51:56,347
as much as I was...

762
00:51:57,835 --> 00:51:58,649
No.

763
00:51:59,984 --> 00:52:01,585
He was...

764
00:52:02,720 --> 00:52:03,988
in even more pain than I was.

765
00:52:06,790 --> 00:52:09,293
The reason I couldn't see
my husband's pain...

766
00:52:11,295 --> 00:52:13,864
was because he kept silent.

767
00:52:16,302 --> 00:52:18,068
In order to protect me, who is so weak,

768
00:52:19,863 --> 00:52:23,900
my husband couldn't even scream
properly a single time...

769
00:52:25,073 --> 00:52:25,876
and like that,

770
00:52:27,277 --> 00:52:30,280
he endured the pain.

771
00:52:30,978 --> 00:52:34,451
Don't touch me! Stop it!

772
00:52:34,452 --> 00:52:36,151
Let go of me!

773
00:52:36,152 --> 00:52:37,287
Baek Mi Young!

774
00:52:50,367 --> 00:52:52,102
Unlike me,

775
00:52:53,567 --> 00:52:55,939
who was busy screaming when it hurt,

776
00:53:00,527 --> 00:53:01,578
my husband,

777
00:53:03,380 --> 00:53:05,015
the more it hurt,

778
00:53:07,144 --> 00:53:08,412
he held it in.

779
00:53:09,053 --> 00:53:10,454
The more it hurt,

780
00:53:11,121 --> 00:53:15,092
he kept pushing it deeper within.

781
00:53:17,628 --> 00:53:18,562
My husband,

782
00:53:20,698 --> 00:53:22,499
even after burying Dal Rae there,

783
00:53:25,402 --> 00:53:26,270
he himself,

784
00:53:28,556 --> 00:53:30,741
didn't go there...

785
00:53:32,731 --> 00:53:34,278
when the azaleas bloomed.

786
00:53:35,543 --> 00:53:39,983
My husband not being able to face...

787
00:53:41,816 --> 00:53:43,120
those beautiful flowers.

788
00:53:45,986 --> 00:53:47,558
I understand it very well.

789
00:53:50,726 --> 00:53:51,662
Because...

790
00:53:53,990 --> 00:53:54,966
we...

791
00:53:56,767 --> 00:53:58,502
are connected.

792
00:54:01,105 --> 00:54:03,373
Through the string called Dal Rae,

793
00:54:05,476 --> 00:54:06,410
we...

794
00:54:09,480 --> 00:54:10,481
were married...

795
00:54:11,982 --> 00:54:13,584
and were parents.

796
00:54:20,324 --> 00:54:21,258
Lord...

797
00:54:22,159 --> 00:54:22,993
Please...

798
00:54:25,162 --> 00:54:26,330
don't...

799
00:54:28,186 --> 00:54:29,800
forgive my sins.

800
00:57:02,119 --> 00:57:03,754
Calvin offered me...

801
00:57:05,061 --> 00:57:07,664
the director position at a new business.

802
00:57:09,219 --> 00:57:11,528
Calvin's starting a wedding business...

803
00:57:12,396 --> 00:57:13,730
and asked me for help.

804
00:58:00,077 --> 00:58:01,693
It's almost over.

805
00:58:01,694 --> 00:58:04,247
So let's not hurt each other anymore...

806
00:58:04,631 --> 00:58:05,649
and end it well.

807
00:58:06,350 --> 00:58:07,451
All I want now...

808
00:58:09,219 --> 00:58:10,354
is just that.

809
00:58:51,528 --> 00:58:54,064
What brings you here at this hour?

810
00:58:58,268 --> 00:58:59,302
Won Ho...

811
00:59:00,804 --> 00:59:02,639
Let's go together next time.

812
00:59:05,075 --> 00:59:06,843
When the azaleas bloom,

813
00:59:08,927 --> 00:59:10,981
let us go together.

814
00:59:15,385 --> 00:59:17,020
I came to tell you this.

815
00:59:34,094 --> 00:59:35,138
Let's go.

816
00:59:39,307 --> 00:59:40,544
Let's go together.

817
00:59:44,981 --> 00:59:46,416
Let us go together...

818
00:59:49,286 --> 00:59:52,022
and visit Dal Rae.

819
01:01:34,445 --> 01:01:37,430
(OK! Let's Get Divorced)

820
01:01:38,858 --> 01:01:42,652
Does he even want
to make things work with me again?

821
01:01:42,705 --> 01:01:43,767
Dangerous? What is?

822
01:01:43,768 --> 01:01:47,037
Would Mi Young's heart change
so easily like that in one go?

823
01:01:47,058 --> 01:01:49,598
You know how much my Won Ho loves kids,
right?

824
01:01:49,618 --> 01:01:53,009
Mi Young, I want to continue
the rest of my life with you.

825
01:01:54,198 --> 01:01:55,151
Don't you know?

826
01:01:55,325 --> 01:01:56,980
I can tear...

827
01:01:57,278 --> 01:01:59,247
Mr. Ji and Ms. Baek apart
as easily as I want.

828
01:01:59,425 --> 01:02:00,784
I can't help but take this all the way.

829
01:02:01,192 --> 01:02:02,352
It's still not too late.

830
01:02:02,758 --> 01:02:05,288
And you still have a chance.

831
01:02:09,027 --> 01:02:11,280
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
